  partName: Blade (7)
  description: The Blade (7) is responsible for extracting energy from the hot gases
    produced by combustion and converting it into mechanical energy to drive the
    engine's compressor. Its unique shape and size allow it to withstand the extreme
    temperatures and stresses encountered in this section, making it a critical part
    of the engine's overall performance. Interestingly, the Blade (7) is often designed
    with a specialized cooling system to prevent overheating and maintain its structural
    integrity, allowing it to operate efficiently in the high-temperature environment.
